@@ -11,6 +11,15 @@ Repositories, code search, issues, pull requests and users through GitHub's offi
 
 Health check: `GET https://api.github.com/user`.
 
+## Results
+
+Tool results reach agent transcripts, so they don't carry the credentials GitHub puts in some responses. REST and MCP results go through the same filter in `results.ts`:
+
+- `temp_clone_token` and `temp_download_token`, the short-lived credentials on repository and runner-download reads, are dropped wherever they appear.
+- A link to a private file's raw content, such as its `download_url`, loses its `token` query parameter. Read the file through the tools instead.
+- A secret-scanning alert's `secret`, the leaked value itself, is dropped.
+- A credential minted because a person asked for one, such as a runner registration token or an installation token, is returned only by the REST tools `results.ts` lists as minting it. Every other result drops those fields, so a token checked with `api.apps.checkToken` is not repeated back.
+
 ## Known gaps
 
 - Release asset upload (`uploads.github.com`) is skipped.
